# Vulnerabilities accepted as not applicable to this application.
#
# Each entry must state WHY the advisory cannot affect spernakit and carry an
# expiry, so a stale suppression fails the gate again instead of silently
# outliving its justification.

# GHSA-qwww-vcr4-c8h2 — react-router 7.18.1 (transitive via react-router-dom 7.18.1)
# "RSC Mode CSRF Bypass Allows Action Execution Before 400 Response".
#
# Not applicable: the advisory is scoped to React Router's RSC mode. Spernakit's
# frontend is a client-rendered SPA built on createBrowserRouter and imports no
# RSC entry points (react-router/rsc, RSCHydratedRouter, matchRSCServerRequest).
# Server-side actions are Elysia routes, not React Router actions.
#
# No patched 7.x exists and react-router-dom has no 8.x line: clearing this
# requires migrating off react-router-dom onto react-router@8, which is a major
# upgrade tracked separately rather than folded into a release.
GHSA-qwww-vcr4-c8h2 exp:2026-10-01
